WEBVTT

00:00:01.040 --> 00:00:10.800
Request from Ichigo... when watching the television, sit a safe distance from the television in a well-lit room.

00:00:09.650 --> 00:00:11.250
First we went to Holland, right?

00:00:14.750 --> 00:00:17.030
Next was to Italy, to the Trevi Fountain.

00:00:19.700 --> 00:00:21.400
After that was the Vatican City State.

00:00:24.070 --> 00:00:26.000
Then, Mont Blanc in Switzerland.

00:00:27.550 --> 00:00:29.130
And we continued here and there...

00:00:29.130 --> 00:00:31.220
How many places will this make?

00:00:31.220 --> 00:00:32.300
Ten.

00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:34.650
And this time it's Germany...

00:00:34.650 --> 00:00:38.250
It sure is fun getting to travel everywhere.

00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:40.060
I've got to thank Henri-sensei!

00:00:40.850 --> 00:00:42.470
Not a care in the world.

00:00:42.470 --> 00:00:43.980
What do you think, Kashino?

00:00:43.980 --> 00:00:44.900
Nothing much.

00:00:44.900 --> 00:00:46.650
You aren't thinking of anything?

00:00:46.650 --> 00:00:51.780
Whatever Henri-sensei is thinking or trying to get us to do, it doesn't matter to me.

00:00:52.530 --> 00:00:55.310
I'm just going to make the best of the situation.

00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:00.720
OP sequence

00:00:57.620 --> 00:00:59.810
What a beautiful castle!

00:01:00.150 --> 00:01:02.150
This is Neuschwanstein Castle.

00:01:02.150 --> 00:01:05.590
It looks like some castle out of a fairy tale!

00:01:05.590 --> 00:01:10.640
Neuschwanstein Castle means "Swan Castle" in German, you know.

00:01:20.850 --> 00:01:24.850
It's pretty from the outside, but the inside is even more amazing!

00:01:28.190 --> 00:01:29.230
What's this?

00:01:32.800 --> 00:01:39.070
fuwa fuwa funwari amakute toro kechau

00:01:32.800 --> 00:01:39.070
Fluffy, fluffy, fluffiness, so sweetly it melts.

00:01:39.070 --> 00:01:44.470
shiawase wo ageru yo yumeiro no pâtishièeru<i>!!</i>

00:01:39.070 --> 00:01:44.470
I'll give you happiness, the dream-coloured Pâtissière<i>!!</i>

00:01:44.470 --> 00:01:49.940
ichigo furejie & furanbowaazu, hapihapi makaron, hapinesu made go!

00:01:44.470 --> 00:01:49.940
Strawberry Fraisier & Framboise, happy happy Macaron, Happiness made go!

00:01:49.940 --> 00:01:55.110
chansu no tobira aketa toki kara kibun joujou ↑ ↑

00:01:49.940 --> 00:01:55.110
Since I opened the door of chance, my mood lifted.

00:01:55.110 --> 00:01:59.070
youkoso suiitsu no oukoku he

00:01:55.110 --> 00:01:59.070
Welcome to the Kingdom of Sweets.

00:01:59.070 --> 00:01:59.990
Bon appétit!

00:01:59.990 --> 00:02:07.370
hajimehane, hetappi demo megezu ni hibishoujin<i>!</i>

00:01:59.990 --> 00:02:07.370
Though I was terrible at the beginning, I was diligent everyday<i>!</i>

00:02:07.370 --> 00:02:10.000
「makeruna<i>! atashi」</i>

00:02:07.370 --> 00:02:10.000
「I won't lose<i>!</i> I said to myself」

00:02:10.170 --> 00:02:11.010
Courage!

00:02:12.210 --> 00:02:17.790
My dream migakeba hikaru takaramono

00:02:12.210 --> 00:02:17.790
My dream when polished is a shining treasure.

00:02:17.790 --> 00:02:20.510
fairy chikara kashite<i>!</i>

00:02:17.790 --> 00:02:20.510
Fairy, lend me your strength<i>!</i>

00:02:20.510 --> 00:02:25.930
shifon, se shibon, juré, bonjuuru, hatsuratsu furuutsu, raburii made go!

00:02:20.510 --> 00:02:25.930
Chiffon, C'est si bon, Gelée, Bonjour, Lively fruits, Lovely made go!

00:02:25.930 --> 00:02:32.020
nakitaku natte mo egao ni nareru mahou

00:02:25.930 --> 00:02:32.020
Even if you cry, there is magic that can make you smile.

00:02:32.020 --> 00:02:37.240
「oishii<i>!」 wo tsukurutte omoikkiri tanoshii ne</i>

00:02:32.020 --> 00:02:37.240
「Delicious<i>!</i>」 and making it wholeheartedly is fun.

00:02:37.240 --> 00:02:43.240
fuwa fuwa funwari amakute toro kechau

00:02:37.240 --> 00:02:43.240
Fluffy, fluffy, fluffiness, so sweetly it melts.

00:02:43.240 --> 00:02:48.580
shiawase wo ageru yo yumeiro no pâtishièeru<i>!!</i>

00:02:43.240 --> 00:02:48.580
I'll give happiness to you, the dream-coloured Pâtissière<i>!!</i>

00:02:48.580 --> 00:02:53.170
ichigo furejie & furanbowaazu, hapihapi makaron, fun fun

00:02:48.580 --> 00:02:53.170
Strawberry Fraisier & Framboise, happy happy Macaron, fun, fun

00:02:53.170 --> 00:02:55.340
yume ni eeru<i>!</i>

00:02:53.170 --> 00:02:55.340
Get them in our dreams<i>!</i>

00:02:55.630 --> 00:02:59.930
Presented by Wasurenai-subs

00:03:00.660 --> 00:03:08.330
It's morning already! Yumeiro Pâtissière is brought to you by Konami and these other sponsors.

00:03:23.820 --> 00:03:24.530
She's returned!

00:03:24.530 --> 00:03:25.550
How pretty!

00:03:25.550 --> 00:03:28.100
This would be the ballet Swan Lake, I believe...

00:03:32.460 --> 00:03:34.740
Makoto-kun!

00:03:34.990 --> 00:03:36.910
I've been waiting!

00:03:39.940 --> 00:03:42.610
Koshiro-senpai, what do you think you're doing?

00:03:42.790 --> 00:03:47.150
What am I doing? I'm dancing to welcome you, Makoto-kun!

00:03:49.320 --> 00:03:53.870
Ojou-sama has been waiting a number of days, preparing this welcome for you!

00:03:53.870 --> 00:03:58.640
For your information, Ojou-sama has practiced classical ballet since she was very little.

00:03:58.640 --> 00:03:59.630
It's perfect!

00:03:59.900 --> 00:04:02.080
I'm so glad you enjoy it!

00:04:02.080 --> 00:04:03.930
I don't enjoy it at all!

00:04:04.360 --> 00:04:10.370
recipe 45

00:04:04.360 --> 00:04:10.370
Bon Bon Chocolat De Tour

00:04:10.860 --> 00:04:16.320
We got letters from Sully-san and went around to various counties...

00:04:16.320 --> 00:04:17.680
Did you as well?

00:04:17.680 --> 00:04:18.690
Yes!

00:04:18.690 --> 00:04:21.110
Team Koshiro also received many letters!

00:04:21.110 --> 00:04:24.160
We went around to all the famous spots in Europe! It's perfect!

00:04:24.610 --> 00:04:29.840
We used my helicopter, however, so we got here way faster than you.

00:04:29.840 --> 00:04:33.620
Yeah, going to different places sure is fun!

00:04:33.620 --> 00:04:38.430
I'd never been to another country unless it was to earn money, so it was very refreshing.

00:04:38.430 --> 00:04:42.530
I was so overjoyed, I can't even remember how many times I broke into Flamenco dancing!

00:04:42.530 --> 00:04:46.340
Yeah... I think I've travelled enough for my whole life.

00:04:46.830 --> 00:04:49.640
Everyone, I bid you welcome after your long journey.

00:04:50.380 --> 00:04:51.570
Sully-san!

00:04:51.570 --> 00:04:53.010
You again?

00:04:53.260 --> 00:04:55.370
Where are we heading this time?

00:04:55.370 --> 00:04:57.350
This is your final destination.

00:04:58.090 --> 00:04:59.680
Henri-sensei!

00:04:59.680 --> 00:05:02.720
Did you enjoy your European vacation?

00:05:02.720 --> 00:05:04.590
Yes, very much so!

00:05:04.590 --> 00:05:06.420
I'm glad to hear that.

00:05:06.420 --> 00:05:09.560
We kind of got the sense we were being led around, though...

00:05:09.950 --> 00:05:12.280
Was there some reason behind this trip?

00:05:12.700 --> 00:05:18.370
It is up to you alone, whether the trip has any meaning to it.

00:05:19.420 --> 00:05:25.640
After your tie, the rematch for the World Cake Grand Prix semifinals...

00:05:25.640 --> 00:05:28.440
...will be held in the castle courtyard tonight.

00:05:28.440 --> 00:05:29.910
Finally...

00:05:29.910 --> 00:05:32.690
The subjects are bon bon chocolats.

00:05:32.690 --> 00:05:34.060
Bon bon chocolats?

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:36.660
Other than that, the rest is up to you.

00:05:36.940 --> 00:05:41.110
Please let your imagination run free, and create a variety of bon bon chocolats.

00:05:42.850 --> 00:05:44.980
Everyone came!

00:05:44.980 --> 00:05:46.370
Of course!

00:05:46.370 --> 00:05:52.390
St. Marie's World Cake Grand Prix is watched closely in the Kingdom of Sweets as well.

00:05:52.390 --> 00:05:55.320
We came to cheer you on before going back to our country.

00:05:55.320 --> 00:05:57.260
We hear you're making bon bon chocolats?

00:05:57.260 --> 00:05:59.320
What kind do you plan to make?

00:05:59.320 --> 00:06:00.620
Umm...

00:06:00.620 --> 00:06:03.340
What are bon bon chocolats again?

00:06:05.250 --> 00:06:08.690
Well, you'll just have to wait until tonight!

00:06:08.690 --> 00:06:11.170
A-Anyway, we're rooting for you.

00:06:11.170 --> 00:06:12.690
Good luck!

00:06:12.690 --> 00:06:14.070
Thank you...

00:06:16.650 --> 00:06:18.770
Move. You're in my way.

00:06:19.710 --> 00:06:21.360
Open a path!

00:06:21.360 --> 00:06:24.260
A future Court Pâtissière is coming through!

00:06:25.300 --> 00:06:28.820
Hey, Marron! Apologise to Caramel!

00:06:26.370 --> 00:06:27.530
Are you okay?

00:06:27.530 --> 00:06:28.820
Yes...

00:06:29.430 --> 00:06:31.830
It's her fault for not getting out of my way.

00:06:31.830 --> 00:06:35.740
You'll never become a Court Pâtissière with an attitude like that!

00:06:35.740 --> 00:06:37.110
What did you say?

00:06:37.110 --> 00:06:40.890
Don't talk all big just because the subject is your specialty, chocolate!

00:06:40.890 --> 00:06:42.910
I'm not talking big!

00:06:42.910 --> 00:06:48.220
I'm saying that your attitude is not appropriate for a Court Pâtissière!

00:06:48.220 --> 00:06:51.680
So then you're saying that <i>you</i> are more appropriate to be a Court Pâtissière?

00:06:51.680 --> 00:06:53.770
How dense can you be!?

00:06:53.770 --> 00:06:55.410
I'm looking forward to tomorrow.

00:06:55.410 --> 00:07:00.070
If you lose a chocolate battle, you'll never become a Court Pâtissière for your entire life!

00:07:00.070 --> 00:07:04.190
I swear by the name of Chocolat, that this battle will be mine!

00:07:04.820 --> 00:07:08.430
Bon bon chocolats are bite-sized chocolates.

00:07:08.430 --> 00:07:14.120
Bon bon chocolats are called Artistic chocolate, and require layers of ingenuity by the chocolatier.

00:07:14.120 --> 00:07:17.160
They are made by hand, one by one, like works of art.

00:07:17.670 --> 00:07:23.590
What's important is the glossy, sparkling chocolate, the various colours coming together, and a beautiful design.

00:07:23.970 --> 00:07:26.970
Then the other charm is the "surprise."

00:07:27.540 --> 00:07:34.190
The inside of a bon bon chocolat is the highlight called the center, as you can't know the flavour until you bite into it.

00:07:34.730 --> 00:07:38.520
What should we use for the center? Which cacao should we combine?

00:07:38.880 --> 00:07:40.950
There are countless possible variations.

00:07:40.950 --> 00:07:45.340
This Grand Prix must be to test our artistic and design sense.

00:07:45.340 --> 00:07:48.470
We have to think very carefully about what to make.

00:07:48.470 --> 00:07:50.210
Oh, I've got plenty of ideas!

00:07:54.440 --> 00:07:59.790
The second I win these semifinals, I'll hold a wedding with Makoto-kun in this castle!

00:08:01.020 --> 00:08:03.120
Which dress should I choose?

00:08:03.120 --> 00:08:05.720
I'll need to change outfits at least 10 times during the reception!

00:08:05.720 --> 00:08:10.780
Umm, Ojou-sama, we'd like to make the bon bon chocolats now...

00:08:10.780 --> 00:08:12.590
I know, sheesh!

00:08:13.420 --> 00:08:15.790
Satou, Shiotani, where are you right now?

00:08:31.700 --> 00:08:33.710
Sorry for making you wait!

00:08:35.210 --> 00:08:36.400
I knew it!

00:08:36.400 --> 00:08:38.550
We've got a full spread, as usual!

00:08:38.550 --> 00:08:40.060
¡Olé!

00:08:40.060 --> 00:08:44.670
I never cease to be amazed at how you do things, Miya Ojou-sama!

00:08:44.670 --> 00:08:48.750
Go and make some bon bon chocolats that can't be beaten!

00:08:49.180 --> 00:08:50.960
Si, señorita!

00:08:51.140 --> 00:08:55.720
You guys do exactly as I tell you, and no slacking off!

00:08:57.630 --> 00:08:59.720
You're going down, Chocolat!

00:09:03.020 --> 00:09:04.440
What's that?

00:09:04.880 --> 00:09:07.280
It's the moon at Mont Saint Michel!

00:09:07.620 --> 00:09:12.080
I could see a beautiful moon the night I danced with Henri-sensei.

00:09:12.080 --> 00:09:15.280
I thought "that would be wonderful made into a sweet!"

00:09:16.290 --> 00:09:17.220
And this?

00:09:17.620 --> 00:09:19.510
This is the hot springs we saw in Italy.

00:09:19.510 --> 00:09:23.570
I thought its terraced field shape would be fun to make into sweets!

00:09:23.950 --> 00:09:27.960
Princess Odette
Koshiro-san

00:09:23.950 --> 00:09:27.960
Swan bon bon
chocolat

00:09:24.260 --> 00:09:27.960
I came up with this when I saw Koshiro-san dancing Princess Odette.

00:09:28.320 --> 00:09:32.920
Maybe we could make an elegant sweet using the form of a swan...

00:09:33.340 --> 00:09:36.980
And this castle is called the "Swan Castle", right?

00:09:37.310 --> 00:09:38.670
I've got a lot more too...

00:09:38.670 --> 00:09:39.520
Then there's...

00:09:39.520 --> 00:09:40.730
Wow.

00:09:41.510 --> 00:09:44.940
You've got all these ideas, one right after another.

00:09:44.940 --> 00:09:46.130
Amano-san.

00:09:46.130 --> 00:09:50.940
Could it be that you were always thinking of ideas for sweets while we were traveling around?

00:09:51.250 --> 00:09:52.590
Yeah...

00:09:52.590 --> 00:09:55.050
I just kind of did it, naturally...

00:09:55.050 --> 00:09:58.370
She never thinks about anything except eating 365 days a year, remember?

00:09:58.370 --> 00:09:59.930
That's just rude!

00:09:59.930 --> 00:10:01.010
But...

00:10:01.010 --> 00:10:03.320
I guess you're kind of like a pâtissière that way...

00:10:05.480 --> 00:10:07.480
But the problem is this.

00:10:07.480 --> 00:10:13.470
I have a lot of images in my head, but how should we turn them into bon bon chocolats?

00:10:13.470 --> 00:10:17.360
Did you forget whose team you're on?

00:10:17.360 --> 00:10:19.860
The Sweets Prince who specialises in chocolate?

00:10:21.740 --> 00:10:25.770
I figured you'd know how to turn these into chocolates, Kashino.

00:10:27.290 --> 00:10:28.770
Well, I guess you learned what I can do.

00:10:32.480 --> 00:10:33.980
What are those?

00:10:34.420 --> 00:10:36.920
This is Italian courveture.

00:10:36.920 --> 00:10:38.620
This is from Switzerland.

00:10:38.620 --> 00:10:40.020
This is from Germany.

00:10:40.020 --> 00:10:42.960
I bought a bunch of them during our trip.

00:10:43.170 --> 00:10:44.640
When did you...

00:10:44.640 --> 00:10:46.770
They all use cacao beans,

00:10:46.770 --> 00:10:51.190
but each country and brand processes them differently, so the flavours vary.

00:10:51.720 --> 00:10:55.090
The best chocolatiers pay special attention to their ingredients.

00:10:55.090 --> 00:10:59.120
I figured it was a good chance to get to know the flavours of many different courvetures.

00:10:59.120 --> 00:11:03.150
So that's what you meant by "make the best of the situation."

00:11:03.150 --> 00:11:09.620
Let's use Amano's ideas and the courvetures from the various locations, and make a world tour of bon bon chocolats!

00:11:09.620 --> 00:11:10.770
Agreed!

00:11:10.770 --> 00:11:12.270
World bon bon chocolats!

00:11:13.940 --> 00:11:16.910
Hey, you guys weren't sitting on your hands either, were you?

00:11:19.220 --> 00:11:24.410
Actually, I took pictures of all the pretty flowers I saw in various places.

00:11:24.920 --> 00:11:29.120
I figured their colour and shape could be useful for making sweets.

00:11:29.490 --> 00:11:35.670
I enjoyed the different flavours of gelato we ate in Italy.

00:11:35.670 --> 00:11:38.850
I thought they could come in handy, so I took notes.

00:11:38.850 --> 00:11:43.100
Okay then, let's cook up some samples right away!

00:11:43.100 --> 00:11:43.970
Kashino!

00:11:44.580 --> 00:11:49.040
Kashino! You've got to, got to, got to win, got it!?

00:11:49.920 --> 00:11:51.320
Sure, of course!

00:11:51.320 --> 00:11:53.190
What's with Chocolat?

00:11:53.190 --> 00:11:56.020
She seems really fired up...

00:11:57.310 --> 00:11:58.860
Yeah, well...

00:12:29.970 --> 00:12:33.220
Eh? Maybe it's not thick enough?

00:12:33.220 --> 00:12:35.170
You put in too much milk.

00:12:35.170 --> 00:12:37.840
Lower the amount of milk and try making it again.

00:12:37.840 --> 00:12:38.880
Got it.

00:12:38.880 --> 00:12:43.170
Sheesh... This isn't one of those "mix it and it's done" things, you know.

00:12:43.170 --> 00:12:45.960
Come on, we're still trying things out.

00:12:45.960 --> 00:12:48.390
And everyone makes mistakes.

00:12:48.390 --> 00:12:50.930
Do you know why it's called "ganache"?

00:12:51.680 --> 00:12:53.230
I've heard the story.

00:12:53.230 --> 00:12:56.250
Ganache is a type of chocolate that was invented by mistake.

00:12:57.640 --> 00:13:02.050
There was once an apprentice pâtissier that worked under a certain master.

00:12:57.970 --> 00:13:00.160
Don't slack off, apprentice!

00:13:00.160 --> 00:13:02.970
Keep working, do exactly as I say!

00:13:02.050 --> 00:13:03.860
Why am I the apprentice?

00:13:02.970 --> 00:13:04.300
Yes, Master!

00:13:03.860 --> 00:13:06.380
I don't have a mustache!

00:13:04.300 --> 00:13:06.380
Now mix in a bit of that milk.

00:13:06.380 --> 00:13:11.520
That apprentice knocked over the milk into the pot by accident.

00:13:06.380 --> 00:13:08.030
Yes, Master!

00:13:11.520 --> 00:13:13.300
What in heavens have you done?

00:13:12.070 --> 00:13:14.740
The master was extremely angry.

00:13:14.740 --> 00:13:17.240
You fool!

00:13:17.370 --> 00:13:21.330
Ganache means "fool" in French.

00:13:17.370 --> 00:13:20.660
You poured in far too much milk!

00:13:22.080 --> 00:13:25.880
But when he tasted the accident, it was surprisingly good.

00:13:25.880 --> 00:13:26.860
Yum!

00:13:26.990 --> 00:13:28.470
Très bien!

00:13:27.990 --> 00:13:32.220
The story about how ganache was born

00:13:28.470 --> 00:13:29.230
Seriously?

00:13:29.230 --> 00:13:31.880
And that's how ganache was born!

00:13:33.700 --> 00:13:37.070
So a new kind of sweet was invented from a mistake...

00:13:37.070 --> 00:13:39.920
Truly, mistakes are the origin of success!

00:13:40.180 --> 00:13:42.030
She might be very clumsy,

00:13:42.030 --> 00:13:47.180
but she can think more out-of-the-box than Kashino or I, since we're so used to working with chocolate.

00:13:47.180 --> 00:13:51.150
Chocolat, you finally understand Ichigo's talents!

00:13:51.150 --> 00:13:55.430
I'm just saying she is useful to Kashino once in a while...

00:13:59.510 --> 00:14:00.940
Finished!

00:14:01.460 --> 00:14:04.940
It's Michaelangelo's statue of David we saw in Italy!

00:14:05.340 --> 00:14:07.330
Wow! It's identical!

00:14:07.330 --> 00:14:09.020
And bite-sized!

00:14:09.020 --> 00:14:11.130
You're really skilled at this, Caramel.

00:14:11.130 --> 00:14:12.950
Aw, you're too kind...

00:14:16.410 --> 00:14:18.920
I guess there's still a lot to learn.

00:14:19.720 --> 00:14:23.410
Caramel, why don't you try adding some colour with this icing?

00:14:23.410 --> 00:14:25.320
That's a nice idea!

00:14:30.070 --> 00:14:31.800
This is my lucky day!

00:14:31.800 --> 00:14:33.820
A starry sky without a cloud in sight!

00:14:33.820 --> 00:14:36.900
This is truly a splendid night to get married!

00:14:37.370 --> 00:14:42.480
Makoto-kun, if Team Koshiro wins this battle, we're getting married straight away, got it?

00:14:43.120 --> 00:14:44.010
Really?

00:14:44.330 --> 00:14:45.050
No way!

00:14:45.050 --> 00:14:46.570
She's just saying that!

00:14:49.880 --> 00:14:52.370
Papa, why are you crying?

00:14:52.370 --> 00:14:53.450
Miya...

00:14:53.450 --> 00:14:55.770
Are you really going to get married?

00:14:55.770 --> 00:14:56.660
Yes...

00:14:57.070 --> 00:15:00.470
Papa, you'll walk me down the aisle, right?

00:15:00.470 --> 00:15:02.960
Makoto-kun is going to make Miya a happy woman!

00:15:03.970 --> 00:15:06.920
Ojou-sama, you look so radiant!

00:15:07.920 --> 00:15:10.430
But... I feel so lonely...

00:15:10.430 --> 00:15:13.160
So do I!

00:15:13.160 --> 00:15:14.260
Gonna cry?

00:15:14.260 --> 00:15:14.890
As if!

00:15:16.460 --> 00:15:19.150
Please pardon the interruption.

00:15:19.590 --> 00:15:22.900
I would like to start the rematch for the semifinals...

00:15:23.330 --> 00:15:25.170
Get it started already!

00:15:25.170 --> 00:15:26.900
I'll win it real quick, and we can have the wedding!

00:15:31.080 --> 00:15:37.330
We will now hold the rematch for the
semifinals of the World Cake Grand Prix!

00:15:38.020 --> 00:15:38.540
Begin!

00:15:46.390 --> 00:15:46.960
Miya...

00:15:46.960 --> 00:15:54.820
Henri-sensei, you had everyone go to various places around Europe before coming here to Neuschwanstein Castle.

00:15:54.820 --> 00:15:56.840
Why was that?

00:15:56.840 --> 00:15:57.920
Yes...

00:15:57.920 --> 00:16:02.040
I wanted to expand everyone's horizons.

00:16:02.040 --> 00:16:08.750
I hope they will come up with new kinds of sweets by using the feelings they obtained while traveling around with their friends,

00:16:08.750 --> 00:16:13.800
instead of just being couped up in a kitchen all the time.

00:16:13.800 --> 00:16:15.330
That's what I thought.

00:16:22.550 --> 00:16:26.620
First, we will try Team Koshiro's bon bon chocolats.

00:16:30.560 --> 00:16:33.420
You used a framboise ganache, yes?

00:16:33.420 --> 00:16:37.540
The deep, bittersweet flavour expands inside my mouth.

00:16:37.540 --> 00:16:42.080
A praline with lemon zest, coated with bitter chocolate...

00:16:42.080 --> 00:16:43.840
Nicely balanced!

00:16:43.840 --> 00:16:47.560
These bon bon chocolats show all kinds of ingenuity.

00:16:47.560 --> 00:16:52.790
I can really sense the feeling of "Making sweets is fun!" from them.

00:16:52.790 --> 00:16:53.740
Yes.

00:16:54.390 --> 00:16:55.240
All right!

00:16:57.670 --> 00:16:59.870
Makoto-kun, it won't be long...

00:17:00.170 --> 00:17:02.570
We'll be married soon!

00:17:04.670 --> 00:17:06.630
This battle is mine.

00:17:07.130 --> 00:17:10.630
Next up is Team Ichigo's bon bon chocolats!

00:17:18.720 --> 00:17:20.640
Banzai!

00:17:29.780 --> 00:17:35.570
Ichigo, from this single chocolate I can feel the wind, the scent, the emotions...

00:17:35.570 --> 00:17:38.280
All the sensations you felt.

00:17:38.810 --> 00:17:39.940
Très bien.

00:17:42.830 --> 00:17:46.330
Team Ichigo

00:17:42.830 --> 00:17:46.330
Team Koshiro

00:17:44.410 --> 00:17:46.330
Team Ichigo wins!

00:17:46.330 --> 00:17:48.340
All right!

00:17:48.340 --> 00:17:49.420
How?

00:17:49.710 --> 00:17:51.090
Why?

00:17:51.090 --> 00:17:52.570
This makes no sense!

00:17:52.570 --> 00:17:54.310
I want to know why!

00:17:54.680 --> 00:17:59.450
Both teams let us have some very novel bon bon chocolats.

00:17:59.450 --> 00:18:01.550
The difference in points was due to the ingredients.

00:18:01.940 --> 00:18:03.450
The ingredients?

00:18:03.450 --> 00:18:05.330
Then there's no way we could have lost!

00:18:05.330 --> 00:18:08.550
We used only the highest quality courveture!

00:18:08.550 --> 00:18:11.110
It wasn't a problem with the price.

00:18:11.110 --> 00:18:18.490
Team Ichigo used ingredients from all around Europe, in order to express a more worldly taste.

00:18:19.150 --> 00:18:24.370
Yeah, we only used ingredients from Château confectionery...

00:18:24.370 --> 00:18:26.630
Well, that's all we had.

00:18:26.630 --> 00:18:28.320
Yeah...

00:18:28.320 --> 00:18:32.350
I could feel a difference in the scope of the images presented.

00:18:32.350 --> 00:18:38.720
I felt like I was going on a European vacation when I ate Team Ichigo's bon bon chocolats.

00:18:38.720 --> 00:18:40.520
What are you talking about?

00:18:40.520 --> 00:18:43.420
We went around Europe, too!

00:18:43.420 --> 00:18:44.770
Yeah!

00:18:44.770 --> 00:18:48.810
Perhaps the difference came from the <i>way</i> you traveled around Europe.

00:18:49.480 --> 00:18:54.780
Compared to Team Ichigo, who took buses and trains from place to place slowly,

00:18:54.780 --> 00:18:59.320
Team Koshiro flew from spot to spot using a helicopter.

00:18:59.710 --> 00:19:02.580
I would have preferred you take your time going from place to place,

00:19:02.580 --> 00:19:06.500
absorb the atmosphere, and use that experience for the Grand Prix.

00:19:07.710 --> 00:19:12.250
Congratulations on getting to the finals of the World Cake Grand Prix!

00:19:13.000 --> 00:19:17.060
Vanilla-senpai, you've just got to win!

00:19:17.060 --> 00:19:17.760
Thank you!

00:19:19.930 --> 00:19:21.260
I lost...

00:19:22.840 --> 00:19:23.930
Marron.

00:19:24.280 --> 00:19:25.370
What do you want?

00:19:25.370 --> 00:19:29.350
Will you let me try your marron flavoured bon bon chocolat?

00:19:30.370 --> 00:19:31.400
Go ahead!

00:19:31.400 --> 00:19:32.870
Let's see here...

00:19:36.100 --> 00:19:42.450
The design is wonderful, and the marron paste ganache center matches the chocolate perfectly.

00:19:42.890 --> 00:19:46.220
You really are an expert at using marron.

00:19:47.200 --> 00:19:49.070
Y-You think?

00:19:49.070 --> 00:19:50.810
I get that a lot, actually...

00:19:51.120 --> 00:19:55.960
Well, since I'm here, I'll try your bon bon chocolats for you.

00:19:55.960 --> 00:19:57.090
Go ahead!

00:20:03.850 --> 00:20:07.770
I would prefer it a bit less sweet, myself.

00:20:07.770 --> 00:20:08.590
But...

00:20:08.590 --> 00:20:10.990
I guess this works pretty well.

00:20:18.830 --> 00:20:21.280
What's wrong with taking a helicopter, huh?

00:20:21.710 --> 00:20:23.930
I'm the daughter of Château confectionery's president!

00:20:23.930 --> 00:20:27.370
Of course I'd use ingredients from my own company!

00:20:27.370 --> 00:20:28.790
Isn't that right, Papa?

00:20:28.790 --> 00:20:30.150
Yes...

00:20:31.120 --> 00:20:34.040
Papa... What are you smiling about?

00:20:34.620 --> 00:20:37.750
Well, this way you won't be getting married, right?

00:20:37.750 --> 00:20:40.520
I still have a long time before you get married.

00:20:41.560 --> 00:20:43.240
You couldn't have...

00:20:43.240 --> 00:20:46.390
You didn't vote for Team Ichigo, right?

00:20:47.010 --> 00:20:48.860
Well, I...

00:20:48.860 --> 00:20:51.900
I am an impartial judge, so...

00:20:51.900 --> 00:20:55.510
I voted for the one I thought tasted better, see?

00:20:55.510 --> 00:20:57.690
Say what!?

00:20:57.690 --> 00:20:59.350
Papa!

00:21:01.300 --> 00:21:03.370
See you later, Miya!

00:21:03.370 --> 00:21:04.570
Wait, Papa!

00:21:05.220 --> 00:21:09.070
Take your time sightseeing, then come home, okay?

00:21:09.070 --> 00:21:10.910
Hey, Papa!

00:21:11.420 --> 00:21:12.690
Geez!

00:21:12.690 --> 00:21:15.330
I hate you, Papa!

