00:23:00.430 --> 00:23:02.490
Dream-coloured Magical Essence!

00:23:03.270 --> 00:23:04.970
Bon bon chocolat.

00:23:06.570 --> 00:23:12.390
Bon bon chocolat are ascetically beautiful yet bite-sized chocolates.

00:23:12.390 --> 00:23:17.990
Inside of it is filling, called center. Well-known centers are ganache, purarine and marzipan, as well as many others.

00:23:17.990 --> 00:23:19.870
It has many kinds of varieties.

00:23:20.880 --> 00:23:26.450
Ganache is finely chopped chocolate melted in boiled fresh cream, and then mixed well together.

00:23:26.450 --> 00:23:29.290
What's unique about this is that it melts right in the mouth.

00:23:29.290 --> 00:23:31.880
Truffles are used this way as an ingredient as well.

00:23:32.510 --> 00:23:37.990
Purarine is roasted almonds and hazelnut mixed together with caramel and melted sugar.

00:23:37.990 --> 00:23:43.930
After it has solidified, it's then smashed into fine pieces, which is then turned into a paste.

00:23:44.550 --> 00:23:51.220
Marzipan is unroasted almonds and sugar mixed together and rolled into a paste.

00:23:51.220 --> 00:23:55.680
It's often used in shapes of humans and animals to embellish the top of the sweets.

00:23:56.250 --> 00:23:59.310
Everyone, which one do you like the most?

00:24:00.230 --> 00:24:02.300
There's a page in a book Kashino borrowed...

00:24:02.300 --> 00:24:07.000
...that's been erased just like the one from Ichigo's grandmother's recipe book.

00:24:07.020 --> 00:24:10.920
And there was Spirit dust that fell out of it!

00:24:10.920 --> 00:24:13.300
What could it mean?

00:24:13.300 --> 00:24:15.050
Well, that's obvious.

00:24:15.050 --> 00:24:18.470
The answer is in the Kingdom of Sweets!

